WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.675
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.945 --> 00:07.988
[protagonist] I was born in Osaka.

3
00:08.071 --> 00:10.240
[♪ light music playing]

4
00:10.324 --> 00:12.284
I think Osaka is an amazing place.

5
00:16.872 --> 00:20.500
It swallows up and absorbs all kinds of people

6
00:20.584 --> 00:21.752
and all kinds of lives.

7
00:21.835 --> 00:24.504
[indistinct chatter]

8
00:27.007 --> 00:29.801
But it never changes.

9
00:32.596 --> 00:36.558
I'm a high school graduate, unemployed, and a virgin

10
00:37.267 --> 00:41.229
with no hopes and dreams. But I'm here too.

11
01:01.625 --> 01:04.461
-[brother exclaims] -[brother's girlfriend] Hey, Yak-kun,

12
01:04.544 --> 01:06.672
your older brother's here, right?

13
01:06.755 --> 01:09.007
-You sure it's okay? -[brother] It's okay.

14
01:09.549 --> 01:11.259
This room is soundproof.

15
01:11.885 --> 01:14.346
Soundproof? I can hear everything.

16
01:16.264 --> 01:19.559
[brother's girlfriend] No... Yak-kun, you can't.

17
01:19.643 --> 01:21.561
[brother] It's okay. It's just the two of us.

18
01:23.689 --> 01:26.400
[brother's girlfriend moans softly] Don't...

19
01:27.567 --> 01:30.404
Yak-kun... you can't do that.

20
01:31.321 --> 01:35.242
[gasps] Hey, hey, hey! Mom, don't just barge in like that!

21
01:35.325 --> 01:37.953
-[mom] Oh, you were sleeping again? -[breathes heavily]

22
01:38.036 --> 01:40.706
What are you doing if you keep sleeping all the time?

23
01:40.789 --> 01:43.583
Crap! What can I do? The store's going under after all.

24
01:43.667 --> 01:45.502
Hurry and get another part-time job

25
01:45.585 --> 01:49.798
so you can at least pay for the rent or food expenses.

26
01:49.881 --> 01:51.591
I've been working nonstop for ages.

27
01:51.675 --> 01:52.717
Okay, okay. I get it.

28
01:52.801 --> 01:54.886
Come on, just get out already!

29
01:54.970 --> 01:56.847
Nothing good ever happens.

30
01:56.930 --> 01:58.974
Because my eldest son is like this.

31
01:59.850 --> 02:02.102
[sighs] Really...

32
02:09.109 --> 02:10.444
[door slides open]

33
02:16.116 --> 02:17.492
Yakisoba again?

34
02:18.410 --> 02:20.454
Mom, your repertoire is way too limited.

35
02:24.416 --> 02:25.917
And there's no pickled ginger.

36
02:26.001 --> 02:28.170
What are you complaining about?

37
02:28.253 --> 02:30.338
Those who don't work shouldn't eat.

38
02:33.133 --> 02:34.926
Try to be more like your father.

39
02:36.136 --> 02:38.638
You want me to follow Dad's example and die from overwork.

40
02:38.722 --> 02:41.600
-Idiot... it's about feeling. -[door slides open]

41
02:43.435 --> 02:46.021
Oh, hello. Sorry to intrude.

42
02:46.104 --> 02:47.814
Yakisoba again?

43
02:47.898 --> 02:50.650
-That yakisoba looks delicious! -I'm over it already.

44
02:50.734 --> 02:55.697
Are you two even using condoms properly? Your mother doesn't know.

45
02:55.781 --> 02:59.618
What are you talking about? That's gross! We're eating outside! That's it.

46
02:59.701 --> 03:02.037
[mom] But I went to all the trouble of making this.

47
03:02.120 --> 03:03.538
There's no portion for Sayaka, right?

48
03:03.622 --> 03:04.748
-[Sayaka] Oh, no, I'm fine. -[phone chimes]

49
03:04.831 --> 03:06.541
-[mom] Why don't we just split it? -[Sayaka chuckles]

50
03:06.625 --> 03:08.668
[brother] I don't get what that means, so let's go.

51
03:08.752 --> 03:11.254
[mom] No, I want you to eat some yakisoba.

52
03:11.338 --> 03:13.340
Oh, crap, I have to get going.

53
03:13.423 --> 03:16.593
Hey, didn't you just start eating a moment ago?

54
03:16.676 --> 03:18.512
-[door opens] -[protagonist] I'm off!

55
03:20.972 --> 03:22.307
Oh, crap.

56
03:22.390 --> 03:25.268
[whining loudly] Oh, crap! Oh, crap!

57
03:25.852 --> 03:30.106
RED LIGHT ELEGY

58
03:41.159 --> 03:43.411
[panting]

59
03:52.754 --> 03:55.257
[exclaims] Gerosuke, you're late!

60
03:55.924 --> 03:58.885
This guy's Kusomaru, right? And this guy's Gerosuke?

61
03:58.969 --> 04:01.179
[protagonist panting] It's been a while, Ishibashi.

62
04:01.263 --> 04:04.975
It's not Ishibashi! You should call me Master, got it?

63
04:05.058 --> 04:07.060
-That hurt. -[panting]

64
04:08.103 --> 04:10.230
[Ishibashi] Hey, have you forgotten how to sit properly?

65
04:15.443 --> 04:18.780
Master, what are you doing right now?

66
04:19.364 --> 04:20.907
[Ishibashi] After graduating from middle school,

67
04:20.991 --> 04:24.703
I worked as a host in Tokyo, but the Kabukicho scene didn't suit me.

68
04:25.662 --> 04:27.497
I just got back the other day.

69
04:28.915 --> 04:29.916
So...

70
04:30.625 --> 04:34.045
-how much money did you bring? -Ow, ow, ow. I brought 2,000 yen.

71
04:36.256 --> 04:39.384
6,000 yen between the two of you is way too pathetic.

72
04:40.468 --> 04:43.054
Well, I'm in university

73
04:43.805 --> 04:46.892
and I have a lot of studying and stuff, so I can't really work.

74
04:46.975 --> 04:49.269
-Shut up, you idiot! -[groans] Ow, that hurt.

75
04:49.352 --> 04:50.604
[Ishibashi's friend] Basshi, you're so cool.

76
04:51.229 --> 04:53.064
-Shall we go to Jankara now? -Mm.

77
04:53.940 --> 04:56.067
-Basshi is so freaking cool. -Yep.

78
04:56.860 --> 04:58.486
[Ishibashi's friend] Basshi, how much do you get?

79
04:58.570 --> 05:01.406
[Ishibashi] It's cheaper than the champagne I had at Princesses.

80
05:02.407 --> 05:03.658
[friend 1] That's unfortunate.

81
05:04.784 --> 05:07.495
If I went to the same middle school as you guys,

82
05:07.579 --> 05:09.915
-I would've been in the same spot. -[guns firing in video game]

83
05:09.998 --> 05:13.001
-Die, die! -[kid 1] Gas seems to be really expensive!

84
05:13.084 --> 05:14.294
[kid 2] Why?

85
05:14.377 --> 05:16.504
[kid 1] Well, a lot of things have been happening.

86
05:16.588 --> 05:19.716
There's no way he's a host in Shinjuku!

87
05:19.799 --> 05:21.217
He's definitely a tout!

88
05:22.052 --> 05:24.429
[friend 2] He's 22 and still leeching off you.

89
05:24.512 --> 05:27.265
I wish a meteorite would hit him precisely and kill him.

90
05:28.099 --> 05:31.353
Oh, by the way, I've got a job at a supermarket.

91
05:31.436 --> 05:33.855
It took a while to find one though.

92
05:34.481 --> 05:35.899
[friend 2] I'm going to become a civil servant

93
05:35.982 --> 05:38.860
and live off taxes of those pigs. Crap, die!

94
05:38.944 --> 05:40.946
I should start one too.

95
05:41.029 --> 05:43.448
-[friend 2 grunts] -My mom's nagging me about money.

96
05:44.157 --> 05:48.328
I don't mind if it's hard work, but I want a job to earn money and meet women.

97
05:48.411 --> 05:50.580
Isn't that just like a host club tout?

98
05:51.790 --> 05:54.125
Satoshi probably gets ripped off though.

99
05:54.209 --> 05:57.754
Oh! There are many jobs paying over 12,000 yen a day.

100
05:57.837 --> 05:59.255
No experience necessary.

101
05:59.839 --> 06:02.425
Transportation job earning 30,000 yen a month,

102
06:02.509 --> 06:04.511
with flexible shifts at two days a week.

103
06:04.594 --> 06:06.096
Uniforms provided,

104
06:06.179 --> 06:10.225
a refreshing workplace with the number of female employees increasing! This is it!

105
06:10.308 --> 06:14.145
-There's nothing but stinky old men. -If there are, they're just primates.

106
06:14.229 --> 06:15.522
[worker 1 coughing]

107
06:15.605 --> 06:18.149
-[worker 2] Hey! Hey! -[beeping]

108
06:19.275 --> 06:21.319
[indistinct chatter]

109
06:25.407 --> 06:26.491
[worker 3] Oh, hey!

110
06:27.701 --> 06:30.912
This is your first time here, right? Yanagawa, right?

111
06:30.996 --> 06:33.498
Ah, yes. I'm Yanagawa Satoshi. Nice to meet you.

112
06:33.581 --> 06:35.125
Can you change into this now?

113
06:35.750 --> 06:39.879
-Right here? -Yeah, there's no space, right?

114
06:39.963 --> 06:42.799
[Inaba] I'm Inaba, the leader, so I'm leaving it to you.

115
06:55.437 --> 06:57.856
-[grunts] Oh, I'm sorry. -[worker] Ow!

116
06:58.732 --> 06:59.774
[tuts]

117
07:01.526 --> 07:02.861
Stand up straight.

118
07:03.653 --> 07:04.779
I'm sorry.

119
07:05.905 --> 07:06.948
[worker tuts]

120
07:17.125 --> 07:19.210
-The hell do you want? -[Satoshi] Oh, I'm sorry!

121
07:19.294 --> 07:20.462
-I'm so sorry. -[tuts]

122
07:27.010 --> 07:29.846
-[drilling machine rattling] -[car horns honking]

123
07:33.224 --> 07:34.893
UNDERGOING CONSTRUCTION

124
07:35.727 --> 07:36.728
[radio beeps]

125
07:36.811 --> 07:37.979
[worker on radio] Okay, I'll start the call.

126
07:38.062 --> 07:40.648
There's a bit of traffic here, so I'll keep it going.

127
07:40.732 --> 07:42.442
[Inaba] Yanagawa, keep a close eye on this.

128
07:42.525 --> 07:43.610
[driver 1] Hey!

129
07:43.693 --> 07:46.112
You're doing some crappy construction work here!

130
07:46.613 --> 07:48.364
How long are you keeping this up, idiot?

131
07:48.448 --> 07:49.949
[Satoshi] Sorry, go on ahead.

132
07:50.033 --> 07:52.035
[bike rider] What are you doing? Let me through!

133
07:52.118 --> 07:53.286
Oh, so sorry!

134
07:55.705 --> 07:57.290
[worker on radio] Yes, understood.

135
07:57.874 --> 07:59.959
[driver 2] Hey, you there!

136
08:00.919 --> 08:03.379
-Come here for a second. -[Satoshi] Hmm?

137
08:06.591 --> 08:10.261
-What is it? -A construction vehicle is coming.

138
08:11.513 --> 08:15.183
Well, even if you tell me to stop, I can't do that, so it's difficult.

139
08:15.266 --> 08:17.727
Construction vehicles have priority.

140
08:18.478 --> 08:21.314
-Stop right now! -[Satoshi] Oh, right...

141
08:23.399 --> 08:24.734
[awkward groan]

142
08:28.613 --> 08:32.200
[awkward groan] It's a bit difficult right now.

143
08:32.283 --> 08:33.451
-[shouts] I'll beat you up, idiot! -[gasps]

144
08:33.535 --> 08:38.122
It's your job to stop the car, isn't it? Stop it like your life depends on it!

145
08:43.336 --> 08:46.172
-[Satoshi whimpers] -Where are you looking, you moron?

146
08:46.256 --> 08:49.676
I'll beat the crap out of you, you moron!

147
08:53.012 --> 08:56.349
The hell you looking at? Got a problem, you idiot?

148
08:56.432 --> 08:57.433
[grunts]

149
08:57.517 --> 09:00.645
Who do you think you are? I'll beat the crap out of you!

150
09:00.728 --> 09:05.024
You brat! Who do you think you're throwing at?

151
09:05.108 --> 09:07.026
-[driver 2] Hey, you! -[truck door closes]

152
09:07.110 --> 09:09.154
-[thwacks] -What?

153
09:10.530 --> 09:12.532
-You little brat! -Come on.

154
09:12.615 --> 09:14.284
[driver 2] I won't show you any mercy!

155
09:14.367 --> 09:17.162
-Come on, you bastard! Let's do this! -[driver 2 shouts angrily]

156
09:17.245 --> 09:19.539
-Die, you bastard! -[terrified scream]

157
09:19.622 --> 09:20.915
Come at me!

158
09:20.999 --> 09:23.793
-[indistinct clamoring] -Hey, hey. Hold on a second!

159
09:23.877 --> 09:26.504
Yanagawa! I'll handle this! You take her

160
09:26.588 --> 09:29.132
and go there! I'm counting on you!

161
09:30.925 --> 09:34.512
-[worker] I'm leaving it to you! -[Satoshi] Ah, yes!

162
09:34.596 --> 09:37.348
[driver 2] Get over here, you brat!

163
09:37.432 --> 09:40.518
[Inaba] Calm down! Calm down!

164
09:47.108 --> 09:50.111
Oh, my name is Yanagawa Satoshi.

165
09:50.987 --> 09:52.113
I just started today.

166
09:52.906 --> 09:54.574
Thanks for earlier.

167
09:55.950 --> 09:59.037
Those kinds of unnecessarily arrogant guys are most annoying.

168
10:00.288 --> 10:01.372
Right.

169
10:02.290 --> 10:03.458
It pisses me off

170
10:03.541 --> 10:05.543
that people talk like that and you can't do anything.

171
10:07.295 --> 10:09.130
No, I'm really sorry.

172
10:12.592 --> 10:15.678
If you're going to apologize, at least show some guts.

173
10:17.055 --> 10:18.056
Right.

174
10:22.018 --> 10:26.981
I'm Chiko. This is my first time doing this part-time job, just like you.

175
10:27.065 --> 10:28.191
Chiko.

176
10:29.234 --> 10:31.861
-Is this your first time here? -Yeah.

177
10:31.945 --> 10:34.530
[indistinct clamoring]

178
10:35.949 --> 10:38.034
[tuts] They're still going at it?

179
10:39.869 --> 10:41.871
-How annoying. -Yeah.

180
10:43.665 --> 10:46.209
No, Chiko, you stay here. Leave it to me.

181
10:46.292 --> 10:48.962
-Huh? -[clamoring continues]

182
10:49.045 --> 10:51.005
[Satoshi] Let's stop fighting...

183
10:51.089 --> 10:52.966
-Ah, let's stop. -[driver 2] You stinky pig idiot!

184
10:53.049 --> 10:55.677
-You idiot! -I'll beat you up, you pig idiot!

185
10:55.760 --> 10:57.512
-[Satoshi exclaims] -[Chiko grunts]

186
10:57.595 --> 10:59.806
[Chiko] That hurt! [groans]

187
11:03.309 --> 11:05.478
[screams]

188
11:05.561 --> 11:07.689
[Satoshi] I'm so sorry! I'm so sorry!

189
11:09.190 --> 11:10.984
[Chiko] When a wimp tries what they're not used to,

190
11:11.067 --> 11:12.485
it goes really bad.

191
11:15.446 --> 11:17.991
I don't care about appearances or anything...

192
11:18.491 --> 11:21.286
but this is just really uncool.

193
11:21.369 --> 11:24.580
No, no, it's fine! Chiko, you're really cute!

194
11:33.673 --> 11:35.925
[♪ cheery music playing]

195
11:39.512 --> 11:40.722
[Satoshi] 'Kay, I'm off.

196
11:40.805 --> 11:43.266
[mom] You worked until morning today.

197
11:43.349 --> 11:45.768
Well, I was suddenly asked to switch shifts.

198
11:45.852 --> 11:47.395
[mom] Aren't you getting a bit too optimistic?

199
11:47.478 --> 11:48.604
It's all right.

200
11:48.688 --> 11:50.440
[mom] Hey, hey. Take this with you.

201
11:50.523 --> 11:53.526
-[soft chuckle] Huh? Okay, thanks. -Take this with you.

202
11:54.360 --> 11:56.529
-[Satoshi] I'm off then! -See you later!

203
11:57.989 --> 12:00.950
-[car horns honking] -[drivers clamoring]

204
12:01.034 --> 12:02.493
[driver 1] Hey, you idiot!

205
12:11.169 --> 12:12.712
[driver 2] You idiot!

206
12:12.795 --> 12:14.964
[Chiko shouts] Who are you throwing cigarettes at?

207
12:15.048 --> 12:18.009
-Hey! The hell you doing! -[indistinct clamoring]

208
12:18.092 --> 12:20.720
What the hell are you doing?

209
12:20.803 --> 12:23.222
[Satoshi] No, Chiko! That'll turn into a crime!

210
12:23.306 --> 12:24.724
[terrified gasping]

211
12:24.807 --> 12:28.436
-Stop it! Seriously! -[yelling angrily]

212
12:28.519 --> 12:30.855
[terrified gasping]

213
12:32.065 --> 12:34.025
[Chiko] I'll kick the crap out of you!

214
12:34.108 --> 12:36.319
Come on! Hey!

215
12:39.572 --> 12:41.574
-Here's coffee. -Break will be over soon.

216
12:41.657 --> 12:44.243
-[Satoshi] Green tea and... -How long are you taking?

217
12:44.327 --> 12:46.954
-[Satoshi] Non-alcoholic beer and... -You're so slow.

218
12:47.038 --> 12:48.623
-Here's your jasmine tea. -[tuts]

219
12:48.706 --> 12:51.417
I said unsweetened jasmine tea, idiot!

220
12:51.501 --> 12:52.752
Oh, I'm sorry.

221
12:52.835 --> 12:55.838
-I'll go buy some. -Never mind! There's no time. Just go!

222
12:55.922 --> 12:57.673
Really? I'm so sorry.

223
12:59.926 --> 13:01.552
[Satoshi] Oh my!

224
13:03.179 --> 13:04.889
I'm so tired!

225
13:04.972 --> 13:08.476
Give it a rest already. Why do you always end up the errand boy?

226
13:08.559 --> 13:10.186
It's not like this place has good company.

227
13:10.269 --> 13:12.772
I guess I'm just born that way.

228
13:14.190 --> 13:16.567
Born to be an errand boy, huh...

229
13:18.069 --> 13:19.612
Excuse me, please stop!

230
13:19.695 --> 13:21.572
-[car engine revving] -Hey, please stop!

231
13:21.656 --> 13:24.075
-[car horn honking] -[Satoshi exclaims, whimpers]

232
13:26.077 --> 13:27.161
[Chiko tuts]

233
13:28.913 --> 13:30.581
[shouts] Give it a rest already!

234
13:31.082 --> 13:33.334
If you don't stop the car, it'll be dangerous for us!

235
13:36.170 --> 13:40.591
You're radiating cowardly aura all over! That's why people underestimate you.

236
13:40.675 --> 13:43.261
-Put some determination in your eyes! -My eyes...

237
13:45.054 --> 13:46.222
Like this?

238
13:48.141 --> 13:50.226
[chuckles] Like that.

239
13:50.309 --> 13:52.687
-That's just funny. [tuts] -[grunts] Sorry.

240
13:52.770 --> 13:55.731
[scoffs] You're such a hopeless case.

241
14:00.153 --> 14:02.905
What you lack is determination.

242
14:03.656 --> 14:07.660
Don't lose! Beat them up! That's the feeling you should have!

243
14:10.037 --> 14:11.372
-[shouts] Okay! -Mm.

244
14:11.956 --> 14:12.957
[tuts]

245
14:21.841 --> 14:23.926
[♪ somber music playing]

246
14:25.386 --> 14:28.055
[kid 1] I wonder if Teru goes to majors next year.

247
14:28.139 --> 14:29.140
[kid 2] Yeah, I think so.

248
14:29.223 --> 14:30.892
[kid 3] Who's Teru?

249
14:30.975 --> 14:32.268
[kid 1] He's the hitter for the Hanshin Tigers.

250
14:32.351 --> 14:35.605
-[kid 3] What's that? -Why am I such a wimp?

251
14:36.355 --> 14:38.858
[chuckles] That's like

252
14:38.941 --> 14:43.571
Tom Cruise wondering why he's Tom Cruise.

253
14:45.531 --> 14:46.991
Tom doesn't think that.

254
14:48.451 --> 14:50.786
Well, you just have to accept reality.

255
14:54.790 --> 14:55.875
No!

256
14:56.500 --> 14:58.586
I want to change myself somehow!

257
14:59.879 --> 15:01.380
I gotta do something!

258
15:01.881 --> 15:04.091
Hey, you guys! It's Ishibashi! Gotta hide!

259
15:04.175 --> 15:06.552
[Satoshi whimpering]

260
15:09.972 --> 15:11.182
Such a liar!

261
15:11.682 --> 15:14.852
[friend 1] That cowardice is deeply ingrained in your genes.

262
15:14.936 --> 15:17.230
It's impossible to change! [laughs]

263
15:17.313 --> 15:20.149
[friend 2] Hey! Stop talking about genes.

264
15:22.944 --> 15:24.237
[passerby 1] Next is my recommendation.

265
15:24.320 --> 15:26.906
-[passerby 2] No rush! -[laughter]

266
15:26.989 --> 15:28.824
[passerby 3] You're drunk!

267
15:28.908 --> 15:32.161
[Satoshi] Oh, excuse me, but you should go take the detour.

268
15:32.245 --> 15:34.455
-[passerby 1] Huh? Cormorant? -[Satoshi] Yes.

269
15:34.538 --> 15:36.707
If you're raising cormorants, that's a pain!

270
15:36.791 --> 15:39.585
-[laughs] -We want to go this way! Let us through!

271
15:40.169 --> 15:42.546
I'm really sorry, but that's impossible.

272
15:42.630 --> 15:44.799
Let us through, you idiot!

273
15:44.882 --> 15:46.467
-[Chiko] What's going on? -[passerby 3] Huh?

274
15:47.051 --> 15:50.179
[chuckles] Whoa! There's a girl?

275
15:50.263 --> 15:53.224
-Well, isn't she cute? -She's pretty cute, isn't she?

276
15:53.307 --> 15:55.893
-[passerby 2] Oh, and she's a blonde! -[laughter]

277
15:55.977 --> 15:58.354
Get outta here and go home, good-for-nothing!

278
15:58.980 --> 16:00.314
I'll beat you up.

279
16:00.398 --> 16:04.360
Oh, so scary! I'm awake now!

280
16:04.443 --> 16:06.696
Yeah, Mr. Hama, maybe this is your type.

281
16:06.779 --> 16:08.948
-[Hama] Yeah, you're probably right! -[laughter continues]

282
16:09.031 --> 16:11.701
[Hama] Well, let's go together!

283
16:11.784 --> 16:14.662
You can't go through here, so please take a detour!

284
16:14.745 --> 16:17.498
-I'm sorry! I'm really sorry! -[thwacks]

285
16:17.581 --> 16:21.127
-I'm really sorry! Really sorry! -[exclaiming]

286
16:21.210 --> 16:23.004
[Hama] He's kind of gross.

287
16:23.671 --> 16:26.173
-[passerby 3] Yeah, he's gross. -Let's just go!

288
16:28.175 --> 16:29.385
[passerby 3] Are you okay, Mr. Hama?

289
16:33.264 --> 16:35.933
That was pretty spirited.

290
16:38.144 --> 16:41.397
Really? [breathing heavily]

291
16:50.448 --> 16:53.326
Hey, there's something I want to tell you.

292
16:54.577 --> 16:55.786
What is it?

293
16:55.870 --> 16:58.289
I'm quitting this part-time job.

294
16:58.873 --> 17:01.292
-Huh? -[Chiko] Not right away though.

295
17:01.959 --> 17:03.711
Once I get my driver's license.

296
17:03.794 --> 17:05.880
I wanted the money then.

297
17:07.006 --> 17:09.342
Is that so?

298
17:12.303 --> 17:15.389
[Chiko] You missed the train, right? Want to come to my place?

299
17:17.308 --> 17:18.476
Huh?

300
17:19.810 --> 17:21.145
I'll give you a ride.

301
17:24.899 --> 17:25.900
Okay.

302
17:25.983 --> 17:27.985
[engine idling]

303
17:34.825 --> 17:38.245
-You're about to fall, so hold on tight. -Got it.

304
17:40.081 --> 17:42.083
[engine revving]

305
17:43.084 --> 17:45.086
[♪ gentle music playing]

306
18:23.040 --> 18:25.459
-We're here. -[dog barking in distance]

307
18:45.855 --> 18:47.440
[Chiko] My mom makes screws

308
18:48.315 --> 18:49.859
and stuff like that.

309
18:49.942 --> 18:51.193
[Satoshi exclaims]

310
19:08.878 --> 19:10.296
[door opens]

311
19:12.590 --> 19:13.966
[Chiko] So tired...

312
19:20.556 --> 19:23.684
I'm going to take a shower. You want to go after?

313
19:23.768 --> 19:25.644
No, I'm fine!

314
19:26.562 --> 19:29.940
Okay, then you can go to sleep over there.

315
19:32.443 --> 19:33.736
Over there...

316
19:50.628 --> 19:53.297
[water running in distance]

317
20:03.307 --> 20:06.227
[breathes nervously]

318
20:09.855 --> 20:12.483
I wonder if I'm going to have sex.

319
20:25.788 --> 20:27.873
[birds chirping]

320
20:40.302 --> 20:41.595
[exclaims loudly] Huh?

321
20:41.679 --> 20:43.681
[machine whirring]

322
20:49.228 --> 20:53.983
Oh, you're awake. Perfect timing. Let's have lunch. Just wait a moment.

323
20:54.066 --> 20:55.192
[Satoshi] Okay.

324
20:56.610 --> 20:57.778
You were fast asleep.

325
20:57.862 --> 21:00.489
Oh, sorry. I fell asleep quick.

326
21:00.573 --> 21:03.576
[Chiko] It's okay. You must've been tired working hard yesterday.

327
21:06.704 --> 21:07.705
[sizzling]

328
21:07.788 --> 21:11.959
-That's rare! I can't believe you made it. -Shut up, old hag.

329
21:12.042 --> 21:15.129
Stop calling me "old hag." I'm still in my 40s.

330
21:15.212 --> 21:17.798
-You're old from 70 onwards. -[Chiko] Yeah, yeah.

331
21:18.424 --> 21:20.175
[chopping]

332
21:29.643 --> 21:31.312
[groans, grunting]

333
21:32.563 --> 21:35.983
[groaning, spits]

334
21:36.066 --> 21:40.279
[Chiko's mom] What is this? It's a lump of salt!

335
21:40.362 --> 21:41.906
[Chiko] I got the portions wrong.

336
21:41.989 --> 21:44.158
You don't have to force yourself to eat it.

337
21:44.241 --> 21:47.119
No, this is just right for me.

338
21:47.703 --> 21:49.330
I'll eat it.

339
21:50.581 --> 21:55.169
You're a funny kid! [chuckles]

340
21:55.252 --> 21:57.963
You're not the type that Chiko has around.

341
21:58.047 --> 22:00.299
-[Satoshi] Is that so? -Yeah.

342
22:00.382 --> 22:02.593
This girl ran away from home recently,

343
22:02.676 --> 22:06.013
but was living with this determined guy. What was his name again?

344
22:06.096 --> 22:07.890
Yusaku, he's in prison now, right?

345
22:07.973 --> 22:09.266
Don't say stupid things.

346
22:10.643 --> 22:13.979
[Chiko's mom] You're the type who'd get beat up by Chiko.

347
22:14.063 --> 22:17.775
If you're going to date her, maybe you should learn to fight.

348
22:18.859 --> 22:20.486
[Chiko] Hey, seriously, stop it.

349
22:21.320 --> 22:22.655
It's not like that!

350
22:23.530 --> 22:25.449
[Chiko's mom] Oh, that's scary. [tuts]

351
22:26.408 --> 22:28.786
Well, I guess that's not really the case.

352
22:29.995 --> 22:31.121
So annoying!

353
22:38.170 --> 22:40.214
-[machine whirring] -[Chiko's mom] Okay.

354
22:40.297 --> 22:44.885
-Let me clean up. -[chuckles] You don't have to do that.

355
22:44.969 --> 22:46.512
[Chiko] You should go home and rest.

356
22:46.595 --> 22:49.848
Well, you let me stay the night and treated me to a meal,

357
22:49.932 --> 22:51.350
so I'll help out.

358
22:57.856 --> 23:00.109
[Chiko's mom] Well, you're being serious, aren't you?

359
23:00.192 --> 23:02.528
You're being persistent. I told you it's not like that.

360
23:02.611 --> 23:06.615
I'm just messing with you.

361
23:06.699 --> 23:08.951
[Chiko's mom] You get upset too easily. [tuts]

362
23:12.329 --> 23:13.831
Excuse me!

363
23:15.541 --> 23:17.543
[debt collector] It's been a while,

364
23:17.626 --> 23:20.004
so I'd like to get at least the interest back today!

365
23:28.971 --> 23:32.224
[debt collector shouts] Hey, are you even listening to me? Pay up!

366
23:33.267 --> 23:38.188
KASUDON

367
23:38.272 --> 23:40.357
[♪ light music playing]

368
23:51.952 --> 23:53.454
[slurping]

369
23:53.537 --> 23:57.291
I LOVE KASUDON

370
23:58.542 --> 23:59.626
So good.

371
23:59.710 --> 24:02.796
KASUDON

372
24:02.880 --> 24:05.299
[♪ closing theme music playing]

373
24:30.240 --> 24:35.245
[inaudible]
